# The Lean WASM runtime IS committed. It is not an optional extra: the course
# is a workbook whose exercises are checked by a real Lean kernel in the
# reader's browser, so a clone without it is a book about proofs rather than a
# place to write them. 213 MiB, largest file 96 MiB — under GitHub's 100 MiB
# limit, so it needs no LFS. site/tools/fetch-lean-wasm.sh still reproduces it.
#
# lean-lib/ is the exception, and it is 1885 files and 76 MiB of them. The
# startup snapshot carries the whole imported Init environment, so the runtime
# never reads a single .olean — verified by running the harness with NO_LIB=1,
# and the reason pack-for-phone.sh leaves them out too.
site/lean-wasm/lean-lib/

# Lean build output
.lake/
*.olean
*.ilean
build/

# editors / OS
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# scratch
/tmp/
*.log

# transient harness state
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# stray Lean scratch files at the repo root
/*.lean

# self-signed dev certificate
site/tools/.cert/

# build outputs — reproducible, and heavy enough to ruin a clone
/workbook-for-phone.tar.gz          # site/tools/pack-for-phone.sh
/separation-logic-site.tar.gz       # tar czf … site
/separation-logic-workbook.html     # site/tools/e2/bundle.mjs
